THE PROTECTED BRIDGE\
\
What a person experiences\
\
Features can save and retrieve information, inspect selected files, use the assistant,\
open native pickers, and interact with local resources. They do this without giving the\
visible web interface unrestricted access to the computer.\
\
What makes it work\
\
Electron is the desktop wrapper that keeps the visible page separate from code allowed to\
use macOS and local files. Electron loads preload.js between those two parts in a protected\
context. That file places named operations on window.api and window.briizy. Those operations\
are the existing frontend connector.\
\
The bridge already covers settings, workspace state, tasks, calendar placements,\
organizer entries, notes, journals, conversations, memory, logs, automation, canvases,\
media, Forest, files, GitHub, model configuration, assistant streaming, health information,\
and screen memory.\
\
The redesign should continue to call this bridge. It should not copy v3's Firestore-backed\
data holders or invent a second data route.\
\
