THE DESKTOP PROCESS AND LOCAL STORAGE\
\
What a person experiences\
\
Information remains available between launches. The assistant can use local context.\
The application can read approved files, open other applications, select media, watch\
attached drives, and operate Briizy screen memory.\
\
What makes it work\
\
electron/main.js creates desktop windows and owns operations that the visible interface\
should not perform directly. It starts the database, assistant, automation, system\
integrations, USB watcher, screen-memory runtime, and the separate Briizy avatar window.\
\
The primary structured store is a SQLite database named briizos.db in Electron's\
application-data directory. SQLite is a local database held in a file. LocalDataService\
opens it and applies the ordered database-upgrade files. The database contains workspace\
state and content such as tasks, organizer entries, canvases, journals, conversations,\
assistant memory, screen-memory session records, automation runs, settings, and logs.\
\
There are current storage exceptions that the redesign must preserve before consolidating\
them. Forest's board lives in forest.library.json. Briizy screenshot files live under the\
application-data rewind/frames directory while their searchable records live in SQLite.\
Launcher layout, muted log kinds, and some theme fallbacks still use the visible page's\
private local storage. Inventory those keys in MAP.txt before moving their owners. Move\
them into the local settings store during their workflow step, but do not erase the old\
value until the converted value has been read back successfully.\
\
The Prisma file is only a developer reference describing data. It does not read or write\
the running application database.\
\
The current workspace record stores masonry columns, stacks, and tile sizes. The ambient\
workspace will need a new local record for window position, window size, front-to-back\
order, minimized state, and the application shown in each window. The existing masonry\
save function cannot accept that new shape without a direct extension.\
\
