CURRENT FEATURES GROUPED BY HUMAN PURPOSE\
\
\
CONVERSATION, SOURCES, AND ASSISTANT ACTIONS\
\
What a person experiences\
\
The Interaction surface supports day planning, general conversation, research, coding,\
and report writing. A person can attach selected source files, receive streamed responses,\
answer clarification questions, approve or reject an action, reopen conversation history,\
choose a model, and inspect what the assistant is doing.\
\
Sources lets a person browse local folders, iCloud Drive, attached USB drives, and GitHub.\
A file can be selected or dragged into a conversation as context. Sources also displays\
activity and evidence records. Google Drive displays connection placeholders, but its\
browsing and download operations are not implemented and must not be described as a\
working feature.\
\
What makes it work\
\
InteractionPanel.jsx draws the conversation. useChat.js restores and saves conversation\
history, sends a turn, and receives streamed output. The assistant runs inside Electron,\
not in the visible React page. ToolContext applies the current allow, confirm, or block\
rules. useToolBridge carries requested interface actions back to the visible application.\
\
SourcesPanel.jsx and FileTree.jsx draw the source browser. The Electron filesystem and\
GitHub modules perform the actual reads. useAppContext supplies a current local snapshot\
of notes, tasks, calendar entries, and projects to the assistant independently of their\
screen position.\
