\
REMEMBERING, FINDING, AND WRITING\
\
What a person experiences\
\
Sticky Notes provides a drawer of notes. A note can be pulled out, moved, resized, and\
returned to the drawer.\
\
Journals provides a bookshelf, templates, pages, rich text, images, trackers, task lists,\
prompts, dashboards, groups, search, linked Forest files, import, and a separately movable\
journal view.\
\
Notefalls combines manually written memory cards with Briizy screen-memory sessions. It\
supports writing, editing, date browsing, searching saved cards and captured text,\
reviewing sessions, opening captured results, and accepting or rejecting proposed actions.\
\
Briizy controls local capture, text recognition, session grouping, search, proposals,\
learning, goals, and daily summaries. Capture remains off until it is explicitly enabled.\
A privacy gate evaluates applications and windows before material is retained.\
\
What makes it work\
\
The written content and search operations use the local bridge and SQLite. The current\
Sticky Notes and Journal Float implementations also own their own outer frames, dragging,\
resizing, and positions. Those presentation behaviors should be removed only after the\
ambient window manager supplies them.\
\
Briizy screen capture uses a native Swift helper, which is a genuine language and process\
boundary. The Briizy avatar is also a separate transparent Electron window with its own\
visible document. Neither should be folded into the main React workspace file.\
