MEDIA AND VISUAL WORK SURFACES\
\
What a person experiences\
\
Media accepts audio or video through a native picker, browser file selection, or drag and\
drop. It restores the queue and playback state and supports play, remove, volume, repeat,\
and shuffle.\
\
Canvases are saved work surfaces created from generated code, a web address, or a local\
file. Their content appears in an isolated frame or Electron web view. The current shell\
lets a canvas choose tiled or floating presentation.\
\
briiZtorm is a standalone visual application shown inside a full-screen overlay. It passes\
saved state to the React shell through browser messages.\
\
Studio opens configured local applications, folders, or web addresses.\
\
What makes it work\
\
The media queue, canvas records, and native operations are reusable. Their current tile,\
floating, position, dragging, and outer-frame rules belong to the old presentation and\
should move to the ambient window manager.\
\
Canvas content and briiZtorm remain isolated documents because that isolation is how they\
execute. Their host controls belong inside the main workspace file; their documents do not.\
