HOW BRIIZOS.V3'S INTERFACE WORKS\
\
Plain-language summary\
\
briizOS.v3 does not create a separate native Mac window for every visible panel. It creates\
one transparent Electron window that covers the usable screen and remains above ordinary\
application windows while shown. React panels move inside that transparent host. Empty\
parts of the host let clicks pass through to the desktop and other applications underneath.\
\
Each visible panel has one shared record containing what it displays, where it sits, how\
large it is, whether it is minimized, and whether it is in front of or behind another\
panel. The shared frame owns dragging, resizing, focus, minimize, close, title treatment,\
and the resize handle. Application content does not own those behaviors.\
\
The bottom launcher opens an application or focuses an existing one. Minimized panels\
appear in a small dock. The launcher can expand into an assistant input.\
\
