WHAT V3 CONTRIBUTES, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT\
\
Use v3 as the authority for the ambient form:\
\
- one transparent, screen-sized host;\
- desktop clicks passing through empty space;\
- independently movable application windows;\
- one account of open, active, minimized, positioned, and sized windows;\
- one bottom launcher and one minimized-window dock;\
- one shared outer frame;\
- a dark translucent surface, detached capsule title bar, restrained edge, blur, and shadow;\
- a small, coherent color and typography vocabulary.\
\
Do not copy v3's folder structure, layers of shared data wrappers, Firebase login, Firestore storage,\
exact coordinates, arbitrary default dimensions, local-storage choices, icon library, or\
unfinished context-menu actions.\
\
V3 does not currently save its window arrangement. Its panel list begins empty after a\
reload. Firestore save functions exist but are not connected to the panel state. The local\
redesign must add real local persistence rather than claim this is already wired.\
\
V3 also allows windows to be lost beyond the screen edge. Its green title-bar control does\
nothing, pin merely disables dragging, and several context-menu commands are visual only.\
These are reference-code limitations, not behaviors to reproduce.\
