PROPOSED AMBIENT EXPERIENCE\
\
Plain-language summary\
\
The application will feel like v3: the Mac desktop remains visible, local features open as\
independent translucent windows, and one bottom launcher opens, focuses, minimizes, and\
restores them. It will still do what local does. The redesign changes how those features\
are reached and arranged, not what information they own.\
\
\
STARTING AND LEAVING THE WORKSPACE\
\
The ambient workspace opens locally without a login gate. It restores the last locally\
saved arrangement. If no arrangement exists, it shows only the launcher. No feature\
window opens until it is selected.\
\
Extend the existing Briizy menu-bar item with Show or Hide Workspace and add a workspace\
keyboard shortcut for the same action. Use Command-Shift-Space on macOS. V3 uses\
Command-Shift-B, but local already uses that key combination for briiZtorm; the existing\
briiZtorm shortcut must remain unchanged. This keeps one menu-bar icon. Briizy capture and\
avatar actions remain in their own labeled section of that menu. Quitting still shuts down\
the local services cleanly.\
\
Empty screen areas pass clicks to the desktop underneath. Every visible interactive area,\
including menus, launcher expansions, dialogs, notices, resize controls, Briizy controls,\
and detached drawers, must explicitly receive clicks.\
\
\
NATIVE HOST DECISIONS\
\
Use one native workspace window, not one native window per feature and not one workspace\
window per display.\
\
The host covers the usable area of one selected display. At first launch it uses the\
primary display. The existing menu-bar item contains Move Workspace to Current Display. That\
command uses the display containing the pointer, moves the host to that display, and keeps\
every feature window inside it. Store feature positions relative to the host's upper-left\
corner, so a display located to the left of the primary display does not give feature\
windows negative saved positions.\
\
If the selected display disappears, move the host to the primary display and bring every\
feature window back inside its usable area. If display dimensions change, retain relative\
placement where possible and apply Return Home only to windows that no longer fit.\
\
While shown, the host remains above ordinary application windows. Clicking another\
application through empty space does not lower the ambient feature windows. The host hides\
only through the menu-bar command, the workspace keyboard shortcut, or application\
quit; losing keyboard focus does not hide it.\
\
Keep the briizOS Dock icon visible. Make the host visible on ordinary macOS Spaces but not\
over a native full-screen application. Revealing it from the Dock, menu bar, or shortcut brings\
it to the current ordinary Space. Do not copy v3's skipTaskbar setting or use an accessory\
activation mode that hides the Dock icon. Briizy keeps its own independent window and its\
capture controls remain in the shared menu-bar item.\
\
These decisions must be implemented in electron/main.js, not simulated only in the visible\
page. Transparent framing, remaining above other applications, display bounds, Dock\
presence, and macOS Space behavior are native window properties.\
\
\
