Theme values will be named only for visible jobs the interface actually needs. Those jobs\
include desktop background, window surface, raised surface, strong text, quiet text,\
primary emphasis, secondary emphasis, success, warning, destructive action, focus edge,\
type, blur, shadow, motion, main-window corners, and capsule corners.\
\
There is no predetermined target count. If two values do the same visible job, combine\
them. If a real state cannot be communicated correctly with the existing values, add the\
smallest direct value beside the theme map. Do not hide a growing visual system in scattered\
hardcoded colors merely to keep a count low.\
